#!/usr/bin/env sh
# Print mandatory follow-up after git pull on vm23.
#
# A here-doc on purpose. MASTER/bin/operator post-pull and data/operator.yml both
# run this, and the steps are an order for a person rather than data a program
# reads: generating fifteen lines from YAML adds a reader to keep in step and
# changes nothing anyone sees. operator status prints one next command for the
# checkout it stands in, not the five-step order a pull on vm23 leaves to follow,
# so it does not replace this.
set -eu

ROOT="$(CDPATH= cd -- "$(dirname -- "$0")/../.." && pwd)"

cat <<EOF
post-pull: source updated at ${ROOT}
post-pull: deployed /home/<app>/app trees are NOT updated by git pull alone.
post-pull: never git stash to force a pull through; a stashed Gemfile.lock took master down.

Next (serial — one app at a time):
  1. ruby34 OPENBSD/bin/vps-state
  2. zsh OPENBSD/bin/vps-deploy <app>     # not vps_ci.sh: it syncs and tests, never migrates or restarts
  3. ruby34 OPENBSD/gates/integrity_gate.rb
  4. ruby34 OPENBSD/gates/health_check.rb --public --all-ready-apps
  5. sh OPENBSD/bin/deploy-smoke.sh       # fast local+public smoke (ALLOW_AMBER_DOWN=1 if needed)

MASTER web changes also need:
  zsh OPENBSD/bin/vps-deploy master

Copy-paste recipes: OPENBSD/data/operator.yml.
EOF
